Z||000000||vinnywolfe||05-15-2000||11:05 PM||||i have an 87 gt that i am restoring.  the engine actually sounds good except for an exhaust leak that i cannot seem to find.  i've checked the ususal culprits; the muffler, the cat, the pipes and can't find anything.  are those 'donut' gaskets in between the upper exhaust pipes infamous for leaking?  if not, any idea's?<P>thanks,<BR>vinny<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Ozzy||05-15-2000||11:16 PM||||The front manifold is notorious for cracking. The 'Y' point of the crossover pipe has gone on my GT twice. Take a piece of tubing long enough to place to your ear and listen with the other end around the drivers side end of the front manifold. (Firewall side) The donut gasket from the crossover pipe to the cat pipe might be a possibility.<P>Ozzy||||reg||1
